---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
import { pathTo } from '../../lib/content';
import { pathTo as sitePath } from '../../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Awesome Goodman, a software engineer interested in software engineering, robotics, machine learning, algorithms, and ideas beyond code."
>
  <div class="wrap about-page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The person behind the notebook</p>
      <h1>
        Hello, I’m {site.author}
        <span class="accent">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>A software engineer, online as {site.username}.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What this notebook is for</h2>
        <p>
          I’m Awesome Goodman. Fieldnotes is my home for writing, project notes,
          and ideas: a place to document what I build, explain concepts, record
          experiments, and work through questions.
        </p>
        <p>
          My main interests are software engineering, robotics, machine
          learning, algorithms, and other STEM subjects. But the notebook has
          room for philosophy, theology, anime, gaming, and whatever else
          invites a closer look.
        </p>
        <h2>Notes, rather than final answers</h2>
        <p>
          The writing here is non-academic. An entry might be a practical
          walkthrough, a record of an approach that didn’t work, or an essay
          around an unresolved question. Updates are dated, and projects leave
          space for decisions as well as results.
        </p>
        <h2>A small, durable home</h2>
        <p>
          This site is built with Astro and local Markdown files. Its content
          lives in Git, and every page is a static file. There are no accounts,
          comments, trackers, or mailing lists. If you’d like to keep up, the{' '}
          <a href={pathTo('rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a> is always open.
        </p>
        <aside class="callout">
          <strong>About the example entries</strong>
          <p>
            The three articles and two projects marked “Example” demonstrate
            Fieldnotes’ content formats and technical features. They are not my
            publications, completed projects, experimental results, or personal
            achievements.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <aside class="about-sidebar">
        <p class="eyebrow">On the shelves</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Software & systems</li>
          <li>Robotics</li>
          <li>Machine learning</li>
          <li>Algorithms</li>
          <li>Philosophy & theology</li>
          <li>Stories & games</li>
        </ul>
        <hr />
        <p class="eyebrow">Find your way</p>
        <a href={pathTo('writing/')}>Read the notebook ↗</a>
        <a href={pathTo('projects/')}>Visit the workbench ↗</a>
        {site.email && <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Get in touch ↗</a>}
        {site.github && <a href={site.github}>Code on GitHub ↗</a>}
        <a href={sitePath('portfolio/')}>Personal portfolio ↗</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
